THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS (used as dependencies, with thanks)
================================================================================
This project runs inference on third-party models and runtime. They are used
under their own licences; VaaniEdge claims no ownership of them. Model ONNX
metadata (`producer_name`, `doc_string`) records the same provenance.

1. ONNX Runtime (Android)        — © Microsoft.            MIT License.
   Maven: com.microsoft.onnxruntime:onnxruntime-android:1.18.0
   Provides libonnxruntime.so and the ai.onnxruntime.* API.

2. OpenAI Whisper (tiny, multilingual) — © OpenAI.         MIT License.
   STT acoustic model. ONNX export from the Hugging Face ONNX community;
   dynamically re-quantized to INT8 and repackaged as vaani_stt_*.int8.onnx.

3. Silero VAD                    — © Silero Team.          MIT License.
   Voice-activity model, repackaged as vaani_vad.onnx.

4. Piper / VITS (hi_IN voice)    — © rhasspy / Piper.      See upstream model card.
   Neural TTS voice (rhasspy/piper-voices). Re-quantized to INT8 and repackaged
   as vaani_tts_vits.int8.onnx; its config as vaani_tts_config.json.

The Whisper Slaney Mel-filterbank matrix in vaani_mel_filters.bin is computed
from first principles (see speech_lab/prepare_models.py) and matches the
librosa/Whisper filterbank definition.
